# CSC1021 SimpleShell Stage 1

simpleshell: src/simpleshell.c src/utility.c src/simpleshell.h
	gcc -Wall src/simpleshell.c src/utility.c -o bin/simpleshell



## simpleshell is the target — the file make will produce.
## The files after the colon (:) are dependencies — if any of these files change, make will rebuild the target.
## it means:
## To create simpleshell, I need simpleshell.c, utility.c, and simpleshell.h.

## gcc — GNU C compiler.
## -Wall — enables warnings; helps catch errors or bad practices.
## src/simpleshell.c src/utility.c — source files to compile.
## -o bin/simpleshell — specifies the output executable inside the bin folder.